        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "\"Blackwork\" or monochrome silk embroidery on white linen was a fashionable embellishment for dress in the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries.  The repeating pattern on this panel displays flora typical of embroideries of the period: honeysuckle, pansies, borage, and grapes."@en ;
